	I took a chance when my priest ran across a pair of cursed rings I was
dying to try out: polymorph and polymorph control.  So I put'em on and found
some things out:

	the higher level monster you become, the less time you will be that monster
	you cannot become a shopkeeper or extremely high level monsters
	(unless you need to be in hell to become a demon-type)

	armor and weapons are real problems!  armor shreds, weapons drop and
you can't rely on wielding wands or pickaxes

	some creatures have great AC (dwarf king) but multiple attacks are
nice too.

	laying eggs takes energy (food)

	umber hulks are fun for mining a level  (rock moles can't carry squat)

	when (as a monster) your hits get low you will become human, not always
convenient when you haven't got armor!

	
	Chests:
	If you haven't found this out already, this is a good tip.
	You can take things out of chests AND you can put things in!  Useful
for keeping the nasties from picking up a weapon and making mincemeat out of
you.  I use it to store unidentified objects and spare equipment.  This is
usually spellbooks that I want to save for a higher level.  It also keeps
pets from dragging things around, although cursed items also work.  Beware!
when you have big pets they will drag loaded chests around.  I like to keep
chests beside altars and I sometimes make the effort to take chests to lower
levels with me.

	Disadvantage: piles have random access, chests have sequential access.
	Solution: use one chest for orc-type stuff (armor, weapons) and another
for magic items.

	Character classes:
	Priest is great when it comes to armor shops!  You just try on all the
uncursed merchandise, and take the best of the lot!

Happy hacking!
